# Copy to core/.env and fill in. core/.env is gitignored; never commit it, and
# never read it into anything under src/ — the browser must not see a key.
#
# Set a spend limit in the Anthropic console before the first call. Not because
# the volume is risky, but because a cap turns a runaway loop from a bill into
# a bug report.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# PostgreSQL, the one store (ADR-001). `pnpm db:up` starts the developer's
# database (compose.yaml) at this address and `pnpm db:migrate` brings it to the
# newest schema. On the always-on host the database is named `openferment`,
# which `pnpm db:reset` refuses to drop, and scripts/host/install.sh writes its
# line once this one is taken out (docs/runbooks/live-host-install.md, step 1).
OPENFERMENT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://openferment:openferment@127.0.0.1:5432/openferment_dev
# The tests make a database of their own for each run on this server, named
# after this address's database (core/tests/conftest.py). This is the default.
# OPENFERMENT_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://openferment:openferment@127.0.0.1:5432/openferment_test

# Optional. The project a command acts in when it names none (ADR-005): the
# nightly job's extraction (scripts/host/nightly.sh), which waits while none is
# named; its checks and check proposals, which act in every project while none
# is named; `pnpm eval`; and the two MCP servers of .mcp.json, which read it
# from here. A project's id follows #/p/ in its address in the app.
# OPENFERMENT_PROJECT=

# Optional. Which models answer, and how hard they think (core/openferment_core/llm.py,
# ROUTES; ADR-008, Implementation 17). Each task family has a default route; in
# plan, explain, extract and judge, Claude Sonnet 5.5 answers where Claude Opus 5.5
# declines or is unavailable:
#   plan (Postdoc's loop): Opus then Sonnet, effort high. Alpha 2.2's model
#     comparison (docs/reports/model-routing-2026-11.md, 8 November 2026).
#   explain (an answer in one call): Opus then Sonnet, effort high, held at
#     extract's route until the retrieval report's answer lane measures it
#     (pnpm lit:report --project <id> --by <name> --judge).
#   extract: Opus then Sonnet, effort high. The rebuild's extraction, where
#     Sonnet answered each of the nine documents Opus declined.
#   index (bulk chores): Claude Haiku 5.5 alone, effort low. The probe's one
#     call; every table of the comparison held index there.
#   judge (an evaluation's grading): Opus then Sonnet, effort max. The
#     comparison's method, with the room its judge's measure set.
# Each setting below lays over the defaults when it is set; leave them
# commented out to keep each family's own. OPENFERMENT_MODEL with
# OPENFERMENT_FALLBACK_MODEL is the chain of plan, explain and extract (the
# fallback may name several models, comma-separated, tried in order after the
# first), and OPENFERMENT_EFFORT (low, medium, high, xhigh or max) their effort.
# judge and index's effort keep their defaults under these settings;
# OPENFERMENT_ROUTES below moves them.
# OPENFERMENT_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# OPENFERMENT_FALLBACK_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# OPENFERMENT_EFFORT=high

# Optional. The model for the bulk chores (OF-BLD-014 E.7): a concept graph's
# batches, HyDE's passage, a question's entity names. It stands alone on the
# index route.
# OPENFERMENT_INDEX_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# Optional. The routing table (core/openferment_core/llm.py, ROUTES), laid over
# the defaults and the settings above family by family: plan (Postdoc's loop),
# explain (an answer in one call), extract, index and judge, each
# {"models": [...], "effort": ...}.
# A model is provider:model in Sci RAG Kit's syntax, a bare id Anthropic's; the
# service serves Anthropic's models, and a route naming another provider waits
# for the owner's decision on how its key is read. `pnpm ready` checks it.
# OPENFERMENT_ROUTES={"judge": {"models": ["anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5"], "effort": "low"}}

# Optional. Spend guards inside the service (OF-BLD-014 D8), in US dollars.
# The daily cap covers every model call in a UTC day; llm.py refuses a call
# that could pass it. The per-question cap bounds one Postdoc question (§5.2).
# OPENFERMENT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=25
# OPENFERMENT_ASK_BUDGET_USD=0.75

# A key that is not scoped to a workspace is accepted only with the workspace
# named on each request (the API answers 400 and says so). Put the workspace's
# id here; it is sent as the anthropic-workspace-id header. Not a secret.
# OPENFERMENT_WORKSPACE_ID=

# A local model behind an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, Ollama, LM Studio)
# may stand in a route as `openai-compatible:<model>` (the owner, 2 November
# 2026): it answers single calls (explain, extract, index, judge) through Sci RAG
# Kit's adapter, at no charge on the day's cap; Postdoc's loop of tools passes
# it over in words. Many local servers take any key.
# OPENFERMENT_LOCAL_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# OPENFERMENT_LOCAL_API_KEY=local

# Optional. The key Sci RAG Kit's REST app at /rag asks of every client, sent
# as `Authorization: Bearer <key>` (ADR-002). While none is set, /rag refuses
# every request; the app itself works without it. Any long random string
# serves, such as one from: openssl rand -hex 32
# OPENFERMENT_RAG_KEY=
